# Conditional viewable tabs — `FLOQRTabGates` only

When a tab must appear or disappear from Firebase datapoints (paid flag, role, affiliation):

1. Load `floqr-tab-gates.js` before the page app.
2. Collect datapoints, then `FLOQRTabGates.bind` / `apply`. Do **not** invent per-page `if (paid) tab.style.display` helpers.

```js
const datapoints = FLOQRTabGates.fromAffiliation({
  user, uid: user.uid, designations, clubsById
});
FLOQRTabGates.bind([{
  tab: "#portalWorkCalendarTab",
  panel: "#portalWorkCalendar",
  when: [
    { datapoint: "serviceMember", equals: true },
    { datapoint: "affiliatedPaidScheduling", equals: true }
  ],
  reason: "work-calendar"
}], datapoints);
```

**Work Calendar** (patron Settings): visible only when `users.serviceMember` is true **and** the user has a non-rejected `clubEmployeeDesignations` row on a club with `clubLocations.staffSchedulingPaid === 1`. Source datapoints stay on those collections (`workCalendarEligible` is derived, 0|1).

**Services & Service Members** (patron Settings): the tab is hidden when `users.IsPatron` is truthy (`1` / `yes` / `true`). It appears when `users.IsServiceMember` or `users.IsserviceMember` (or legacy `serviceMember`) is truthy **and** `IsPatron` is `0` / `no`. Patrons elect from My Profile; that write sets `IsPatron=0` and `IsServiceMember=1`. **Review & elect** subtab still requires `isClubAdmin`.

**Forbidden:** hiding tabs with one-off CSS `display:none` in the page app; leaving a gated tab visible and relying on a 404 inside the panel.

Checklist: `floqr-tab-gates.js` loaded; `when` clauses use real datapoint paths; hidden tab is not `.active`; FloqAi/help if the tab is a new patron feature.
